<!--
  Porog (Postern Container) — window base theme for the DPC app shell.

  Porog is a COMPOSE-ONLY surface: the actual Material3 look is drawn by
  PorogTheme (provision/ui/PorogTheme.kt) via androidx.compose.material3, and the
  app deliberately does NOT depend on the com.google.android.material XML library
  (see app/build.gradle.kts — only the Compose bundle is pulled in). So the
  activity window theme must resolve WITHOUT that library: an earlier scaffold
  referenced @style/Theme.Material3.DayNight.NoActionBar, which lives only in
  com.google.android.material and therefore fails resource linking here.

  This local theme parents the platform DayNight theme (API 29+, always present;
  minSdk is 30) and simply strips the action bar / title so Compose owns the whole
  window. Day/night still follows the system setting, matching PorogTheme's
  isSystemInDarkTheme() default.

  SCAFFOLD · DESIGN ONLY · UNAUDITED · never provisioned on hardware.
-->
<resources>
    <style name="Theme.PosternContainer" parent="@android:style/Theme.DeviceDefault.DayNight">
        <item name="android:windowActionBar">false</item>
        <item name="android:windowNoTitle">true</item>
    </style>
</resources>
